# fastly_service_dictionary_items (Resource)

Manages key-value items in a Fastly Dictionary.

Each key declared in `items` is owned by this Terraform resource. Terraform
creates missing managed keys, updates managed values that drift, and deletes a
managed key when it is removed from the `items` map.

Items that are not declared in this resource are left unchanged. This allows a
Dictionary to contain Terraform-managed items alongside items managed by other
systems, the Fastly API, the Fastly CLI, or the Fastly control panel.

Dictionary items are versionless and immediately visible to the linked
service, regardless of which version is active.

## Limitations

- `write_only` dictionaries are not supported: their items cannot be read back
  from the API, so Terraform cannot detect or reconcile drift for them.

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_cdn_auto" "example" {
  name          = "example-service"
  force_destroy = true

  domain {
    name = "example.com"
  }

  dictionary {
    name = "application_configuration"
  }
}

resource "fastly_service_dictionary_items" "example" {
  service_id    = fastly_service_cdn_auto.example.id
  dictionary_id = fastly_service_cdn_auto.example.dictionary[0].dictionary_id

  items = {
    environment = "production"
    feature_x   = "enabled"
    api_version = "v2"
  }
}
```

Removing a key from `items` deletes that key from the Dictionary:

```terraform
resource "fastly_service_dictionary_items" "example" {
  service_id    = fastly_service_cdn_auto.example.id
  dictionary_id = fastly_service_cdn_auto.example.dictionary[0].dictionary_id

  items = {
    environment = "production"
    api_version = "v2"
  }
}
```

In this example Terraform deletes the previously managed `feature_x` item, but
does not delete unrelated Dictionary items that were never managed by this
resource.

